Bug in backend/mmc/store/event_store.py (M1): tests/test_chain_properties.py::test_single_byte_mutation_fails_verification fails with --hypothesis-seed=2. It is NOT a flake. Cause: a single-byte change to the JSONL can leave the parsed event semantically identical (e.g. the last digit of a float like 6.3373105101272424e+16 changed so it parses to the same double; also possibly escape/encoding variants), so recomputing hashes from the parsed event still passes.

Fix: verify_chain() must also require each stored line's raw bytes to equal the canonical serialization of the parsed event (the exact bytes append() writes). Make append() write exactly that canonical form so the check holds. Add a deterministic regression test that alters the final digit of a float in a stored line without changing its parsed value and asserts verify_chain() is False. Then run `uv run pytest -q tests/test_chain_properties.py --hypothesis-seed=N` for N in 1..60 and the full `uv run pytest -q` and make sure all pass. Correct the docs/DECISIONS.md entry that calls this a pre-existing flake. Do not commit. Finish with a short summary and the test results.
